[0;36mออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออ
[1;36m WHAT THIS BOARD KNOWS
[0;37m 
[0;37m Would you like to know more? You would.
[0;37m 
[1;33m THE LINK IS NOT ENCRYPTED
[0;37m You are connected over telnet. Telnet has
[0;37m no encryption. Everything you type crosses
[0;37m the network as readable text: your
[0;37m password, your messages, all of it.
[0;37m 
[0;37m Anyone on the path can read it. Whoever
[0;37m runs the wifi you are on, your internet
[0;37m provider, the sysop's provider, anyone
[0;37m between. That is not a bug here. It is the
[0;37m price of letting a 1982 computer call in,
[0;37m because a C64 cannot do encryption.
[0;37m 
[1;33m YOUR PASSWORD ON THE BOARD
[0;37m It is never stored as you typed it. It is
[0;37m salted and hashed with SHA-256, a thousand
[0;37m rounds, and only the hash is written down.
[0;37m Nobody can read it back, including the
[0;37m sysop. Backups redact it.
[0;37m 
[0;37m That protects the file. It does nothing
[0;37m about the wire, where you typed it in the
[0;37m clear on the way here.
[0;37m 
[1;33m WHAT THE SYSOP CAN SEE
[0;37m Your handle, your address, when you called
[0;37m and for how long, and the last command you
[0;37m ran. Staff can watch a node live. Messages
[0;37m you leave sit in a file on the board until
[0;37m they are read. Assume the sysop can read
[0;37m anything on their own machine, because
[0;37m they can. It is their machine.
[0;37m 
[1;33m SO WHAT IS MY REAL RISK
[0;37m Honestly? Small. This is a hobby board on
[0;37m a five dollar chip. It is conversation and
[0;37m nothing critical. There is no money here,
[0;37m no card numbers, no keys to anything. If
[0;37m somebody read every word of it they would
[0;37m learn what you said in a chat room.
[0;37m 
[1;31m There is one real risk, and it is this:
[1;31m a password you use somewhere else.
[0;37m 
[0;37m If you reuse one and it is read on the
[0;37m way here, the person reading it now has a
[0;37m password that works on your email. That is
[0;37m how accounts get taken, and it has nothing
[0;37m to do with this board being good or bad.
[0;37m 
[1;33m SO
[1;32m Use a password you use nowhere else.
[0;37m Make it up here, forget it afterwards. Say
[0;37m nothing on the board you would mind being
[0;37m read out. Then enjoy yourself, because
[0;37m that is what it is for.
[0;37m 
[1;30m Sysops: do staff work from your own
[1;30m network or a VPN, never across the
[1;30m internet. See PUBLIC.md.
